3. GPT ko Foundation padhane ka best method
Yeh tumhari requirement ka sabse critical part hai.

Main Context Compiler ko aise design karunga:
Reading level	Kya read hoga	GPT context usage
L0	Company identity aur basic rules	Bahut chhota
L1	Selected project snapshot	Relevant summary
L2	Assigned developer ki architecture	Sirf ek specialist
L3	Current task aur related source files	Limited code
L4	Deep audit, dependencies aur test evidence	Sirf zaroorat par

Maan lo Backend Developer ko payment gateway banana hai.

Usko poori 8-agent architecture read nahi karayenge. Sirf relevant project requirements, backend contracts, payment-related files, DB tables, security rules aur related test evidence denge.

Naye chat ka context automatically generate karne ke liye product mein Generate Developer Context capability hogi. Tumhe manually poori repository copy nahi karni padegi; abhi normal ChatGPT chat mein generated context packet paste karna hoga, jab tak direct authorized connection available na ho.
4. Audit system GPT ke bina kitna kaam karega?
Bahut saara.
Automatic repository scanning
No GPT required

File inventory, imports, dependency relationships, code hashes, Git changes aur available tests.
Static validation
No GPT required

Lint, types, test execution, dependency vulnerabilities aur secret checks.
Intelligent AI audit
Controlled AI usage

Sirf changed files, critical dependencies aur high-risk decisions ka model-based review.
Audit ledger har result ke saath commit hash, file hashes, test version, findings aur unresolved risks rakhega. File change nahi hui to uska verified audit result reuse kar sakenge, provided dependencies aur test configuration bhi unchanged ho.

Is approach ke liye repository-map aur incremental analysis useful engineering patterns hain. Aider ka repository map aur LangGraph ka checkpoint/store separation is design ko inform karte hain. 
GitHub+1

5. Technology stack — meri final initial choice
Component	Choice
Backend	Python + FastAPI
Main database	PostgreSQL
Agent workflow	LangGraph, controlled use
Persistent execution state	PostgreSQL checkpointer/store
Model gateway	Initially provider adapters; later LiteLLM
Repository analysis	Python parser + dependency graph
Quality assurance	Pytest + static analysis + security scans
GitHub integration	GitHub API and Actions
Artifact storage	Object storage, not Git for runtime data

LangGraph ke checkpointer aur long-term store alag purposes serve karte hain: ek current workflow execution ko save karta hai, doosra sessions ke across persistent knowledge rakhta hai. 
GitHub+1


LiteLLM ko later adopt kar sakte hain. Iske budgets database-backed hote hain, isliye ise sirf ek API wrapper samajhkar integrate nahi karenge. 
liteLLM+1


Main PostgreSQL ko central source of truth rakhunga. Managed hosting choose karte waqt backup aur recovery policy bhi acceptance requirements mein hogi; free database plans par automatic backups assume nahi karenge. 
